engsyn: rewrite the enye to ny before the engine link

User-tuned eci_engsyn.c: Spanish text reaches the engine in bytes the
voice data never learned, so a static pre-filter rewrites the enye
(Latin-1 0xF1 / UTF-8 C3 B1) to "ny" -- "enye" standing alone -- and
the capital to "Ny"/"Enye", before the text enters the engine link.
Comment-only removals aside, that is the whole of this patch.
Applied at build time so CI builds the same file.
